  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1120</x>
      <y>1460</y>
      <w>420</w>
      <h>100</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>run() blocks until the answer is ready, so it is only
called on a background thread (see FindAnythingService).
Holds no model client: each call is given the client to
use, so a conversation always talks to its own model.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1850</x>
      <y>1880</y>
      <w>400</w>
      <h>170</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Bound to one model for its whole life (modelSettings,
set when it is created), so text never moves from a
local model's conversation to a cloud model.
Used by one request at a time: the GUI disables
Ask mode input while a request is running.
Tool calls and tool results are kept only for the
request in progress: dropToolMessages() removes them
when the next request starts, and ConversationStore
never saves them.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>2960</x>
      <y>270</y>
      <w>270</w>
      <h>60</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>status is VERIFIED, UNVERIFIED,
or SOURCE_CHANGED.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>330</x>
      <y>300</y>
      <w>420</w>
      <h>90</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>One per request. Remembers the passages a search has
given the model, so a later search names the earlier
search in place of the text. A result withheld from a
cloud model (local-only folder) records nothing.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
